# Environment for the self-hosted (OVHcloud VPS + Docker Compose + Cloudflare Tunnel) deployment. Placeholders only —
# copy to `.env` NEXT TO compose.yaml on the server, then `chmod 600 .env`. Never commit the real file. Guide: docs/DEPLOYMENT_VPS.md
# The website has NO database: do not add DATABASE_URL or any database setting (deploy/preflight.sh refuses to continue if one is present).

# --- Compass Tools CRM (REQUIRED) ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same value as the CRM's WEBSITE_API_KEY (>= 32 characters; the CRM operator generates it with `openssl rand -hex 32`).
CRM_API_KEY=<same-value-as-the-CRMs-WEBSITE_API_KEY>
# The CRM Company id (the CRM's WEBSITE_API_COMPANY_ID). Used by the contact form and the newsletter sign-up.
CRM_COMPANY_ID=<crm-company-id>
# Optional but recommended: identical to the CRM's LEAD_INGEST_SECRET (>= 32 characters). Lets the CRM record the visitor's IP / location.
# LEAD_INGEST_SECRET=<same-value-as-the-CRMs-LEAD_INGEST_SECRET>
# The CRM's origin on the private network (default shown). `compass-crm` is an alias the CRM's own compose file must define; the live stack may expose
# the CRM under another name (for example http://app:3000). Set the name that really resolves - deploy/preflight.sh verifies THIS host.
# Plain http is fine inside an internal Docker network.
# CRM_API_URL=http://compass-crm:3000

# --- Notification email (REQUIRED) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GMAIL_SENDER_EMAIL=<the-single-gmail-address@example.com>
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=<google-app-password>

# --- Docker / networking (optional overrides; defaults shown) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two networks that the CRM project already owns. They must exist; compose never creates them. Read the real names with
# `docker network ls` — do not guess.
#   CRM_API_NETWORK_NAME  the internal network that carries ONLY the CRM app, answering as `compass-crm`   (default compass-tools-website-api)
#   TUNNEL_NETWORK_NAME   the network the Cloudflare Tunnel connector is on, so the tunnel can reach http://bft-web:3000 (default compass-tools_web)
# It must not be a network that also carries PostgreSQL.
# CRM_API_NETWORK_NAME=compass-tools-website-api
# TUNNEL_NETWORK_NAME=compass-tools_web
# Image tag, for rollback: APP_VERSION=<git short sha>
# APP_VERSION=

# Set by compose.yaml and deliberately NOT configurable here: TRUSTED_PROXY=cloudflare.
